    "summary": "This celebratory <b>Royal Thai Stuffed Roti Mataba</b> is a festive flatbread feast featuring paper-thin, buttery layers of handmade dough wrapped around an intensely aromatic yellow curry duck filling. Originating from Southern Thai Muslim culinary traditions, this dish is traditionally prepared for special family gatherings, cultural festivities, and grand banquets. The dough is enriched with sweet condensed milk, coconut milk, and rich clarified butter, producing a exceptionally flaky and crispy shell when pan-fried on a blistering hot iron griddle. Inside, rich minced duck leg is slow-cooked with fresh lemongrass, kaffir lime leaves, minced coriander roots, and aromatic roasted spices until golden and flavorful. Served alongside a bright, tangy <b>Ajat cucumber pickle</b> crafted from sweet rice vinegar, fresh red chili rings, and crisp shallots, every bite delivers a harmonious balance of savory, rich, sour, and mildly spicy notes. Master the technique of stretching paper-thin dough and frying to golden perfection for an unforgettable center-piece recipe.",
